\p \v 10 \w On the evening|strong="H6153"\w* \w of the fourteenth|strong="H702"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w of the month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w while the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w were camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w* \w on the plains|strong="H6160"\w* \w of Jericho|strong="H3405"\w*, \w they kept|strong="H6213"\w* \w the Passover|strong="H6453"\w*. \v 11 \w The day after|strong="H4283"\w* \w the Passover|strong="H6453"\w*, \w on that very|strong="H6106"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, \w they ate|strong="H398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w* \w and roasted grain|strong="H7033"\w* \w from the produce|strong="H5669"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w*.
