\s1 The Commander of the LORD’s Army
\p \v 13 \w Now when Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w was|strong="H1961"\w* \w near Jericho|strong="H3405"\w*, \w he looked up|strong="H5375"\w* \w and saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w standing|strong="H5975"\w* \w in front of him|strong="H5048"\w* \w with a drawn|strong="H8025"\w* \w sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w in His hand|strong="H3027"\w*. \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w approached|strong="H1980"\w* \w Him|strong="H413"\w* \w and asked|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Are You|strong="H859"\w* for us \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w for our enemies|strong="H6862"\w*?”
