\p \v 10 \w But Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*: “\w Do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w give a battle cry|strong="H7321"\w* \w or let your voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w be heard|strong="H8085"\w*; \w do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w let one word|strong="H1697"\w* \w come out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of your mouth|strong="H6310"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w I tell|strong="H559"\w* \w you|strong="H413"\w* \w to shout|strong="H7321"\w*. \w Then you are to shout|strong="H7321"\w*!” \v 11 \w So he had the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w carried around|strong="H5437"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w circling|strong="H5362"\w* \w it once|strong="H6471"\w*. \w And the people returned|strong="H935"\w* \w to the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w and spent the night there|strong="H3885"\w*.
