\c 7
\s1 The Defeat at Ai
\p \v 1 \w The Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w however|strong="H3478"\w*, \w acted|strong="H4603"\w* \w unfaithfully|strong="H4604"\w* \w regarding the things devoted to destruction|strong="H2764"\w*.\f + \fr 7:1 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 11, 12, 13, and 15.\f* \w Achan|strong="H5912"\w*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Achan \ft means \fqa troubler\ft ; also called \fqa Achar\ft in \ref 1 Chronicles 2:7|1CH 2:7\ref*.\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Carmi|strong="H3756"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zabdi|strong="H2067"\w*,\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Zabdi \ft is a variant of \fqa Zimri\ft ; also in verses 17 and 18; see LXX and \ref 1 Chronicles 2:6|1CH 2:6\ref*.\f* \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zerah|strong="H2226"\w*, \w of the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w some of|strong="H4480"\w* \w what was set apart|strong="H2764"\w*. \w So the anger|strong="H639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w burned|strong="H2734"\w* \w against the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*.
\p \v 2 \w Meanwhile, Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w from Jericho|strong="H3405"\w* \w to Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w is near|strong="H5973"\w* \w Beth-aven|strong="H1007"\w* \w to the east|strong="H6924"\w* \w of Bethel|strong="H1008"\w*, \w and told them|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and spy out|strong="H7270"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w*.” \w So the men|strong="H582"\w* \w went up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and spied out|strong="H7270"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*.
