\p \v 13 \w Get up|strong="H6965"\w* \w and consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w Consecrate yourselves|strong="H6942"\w* \w for tomorrow|strong="H4279"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w Among you|strong="H7130"\w*, \w O Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w there are things devoted to destruction|strong="H2764"\w*. \w You cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w stand|strong="H6965"\w* \w against|strong="H6440"\w* \w your enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w you remove|strong="H5493"\w* \w them|strong="H2764"\w*. \v 14 \w In the morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w you must present yourselves|strong="H7126"\w* \w tribe by tribe|strong="H7626"\w*. \w The tribe|strong="H7626"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w selects|strong="H3920"\w* \w shall come forward|strong="H7126"\w* \w clan by clan|strong="H4940"\w*, \w and the clan|strong="H4940"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w selects|strong="H3920"\w* \w shall come forward|strong="H7126"\w* \w family by family|strong="H1004"\w*, \w and the family|strong="H1004"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w selects|strong="H3920"\w* \w shall come forward|strong="H7126"\w* \w man by man|strong="H1397"\w*. \v 15 \w The one who is caught|strong="H3920"\w* \w with the things devoted to destruction|strong="H2764"\w* \w must be burned|strong="H8313"\w*, \w along with all|strong="H853"\w* \w that belongs to him|strong="H3605"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w he has transgressed|strong="H5674"\w* \w the covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w and|strong="H3588"\w* \w committed|strong="H6213"\w* \w an outrage|strong="H5039"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.’”
\s1 The Sin of Achan
\p \v 16 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w arose early|strong="H7925"\w* \w the next morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w and had Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w come forward|strong="H7126"\w* \w tribe by tribe|strong="H7626"\w*, \w and the tribe|strong="H7626"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w was selected|strong="H3920"\w*. \v 17 \w He had the clans|strong="H4940"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w come forward|strong="H7126"\w*, \w and the clan|strong="H4940"\w* \w of the Zerahites|strong="H2227"\w* \w was selected|strong="H3920"\w*. \w He had the clan|strong="H4940"\w* \w of the Zerahites|strong="H2227"\w* \w come forward|strong="H7126"\w*, \w and the family|strong="H1397"\w* \w of Zabdi|strong="H2067"\w* \w was selected|strong="H3920"\w*. \v 18 \w And he had the family of Zabdi|strong="H1004"\w* \w come forward|strong="H7126"\w* \w man by man|strong="H1397"\w*, \w and Achan|strong="H5912"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Carmi|strong="H3756"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zabdi|strong="H2067"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zerah|strong="H2226"\w*, \w of the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w was selected|strong="H3920"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Achan|strong="H5912"\w*, “\w My son|strong="H1121"\w*, \w give|strong="H7760"\w* \w glory|strong="H3519"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and make|strong="H5414"\w* \w a confession|strong="H8426"\w* to Him. \w I urge you|strong="H4994"\w* \w to tell|strong="H5046"\w* me \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w you have done|strong="H6213"\w*; \w do not|strong="H408"\w* \w hide it|strong="H3582"\w* \w from me|strong="H4480"\w*.”
\p \v 20 “\w It is true|strong="H546"\w*,” \w Achan|strong="H5912"\w* \w replied|strong="H6030"\w*, “\w I|strong="H595"\w* \w have sinned|strong="H2398"\w* \w against the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w This|strong="H2063"\w* \w is what I did|strong="H6213"\w*: \v 21 \w When I saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w among the spoils|strong="H7998"\w* \w a|strong="H259"\w* \w beautiful|strong="H2896"\w* \w cloak|strong="H155"\w* \w from Shinar|strong="H8152"\w*,\f + \fr 7:21 \ft That is, Babylonia \f* \w two hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w shekels|strong="H8255"\w* \w of silver|strong="H3701"\w*,\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa 200 shekels \ft is approximately 5 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of silver.\f* \w and a|strong="H259"\w* \w bar|strong="H3956"\w* \w of gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w weighing|strong="H4948"\w* \w fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w shekels|strong="H8255"\w*,\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of gold.\f* \w I coveted them|strong="H2530"\w* \w and took them|strong="H3947"\w*. \w They are|strong="H2009"\w* \w hidden|strong="H2934"\w* \w in the ground|strong="H776"\w* \w inside|strong="H8432"\w* \w my tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w with the silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w underneath|strong="H8478"\w*.”
\p \v 22 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w messengers|strong="H4397"\w* \w who ran|strong="H7323"\w* \w to the tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w and there it all was|strong="H2009"\w*, \w hidden|strong="H2934"\w* \w in his tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w with the silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w underneath|strong="H8478"\w*. \v 23 \w They took the things|strong="H3947"\w* \w from inside|strong="H8432"\w* \w the tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w brought them|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w and spread them out|strong="H3332"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 24 \w Then Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*, \w together with|strong="H5973"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w Achan|strong="H5912"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zerah|strong="H2226"\w*, \w the silver|strong="H3701"\w*, \w the cloak|strong="H155"\w*, \w the bar|strong="H3956"\w* \w of gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and daughters|strong="H1323"\w*, \w his oxen|strong="H7794"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w donkeys|strong="H2543"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w sheep|strong="H6629"\w*, \w his tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w and everything else|strong="H3605"\w* \w he owned|strong="H834"\w*, \w and brought them|strong="H5927"\w* \w to the Valley|strong="H6010"\w* \w of Achor|strong="H5911"\w*.
\p \v 25 “\w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w have you brought this trouble upon us|strong="H5916"\w*?” \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*. “\w Today|strong="H3117"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w will bring trouble upon you|strong="H5916"\w*!” \w And all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w stoned him to death|strong="H7275"\w*. \w Then they stoned the others|strong="H5619"\w* \w and burned their bodies|strong="H8313"\w*. \v 26 \w And they heaped|strong="H6965"\w* \w over Achan|strong="H5921"\w* \w a large|strong="H1419"\w* \w pile|strong="H1530"\w* \w of rocks|strong="H68"\w* \w that remains to|strong="H5704"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*. \w So the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w turned|strong="H7725"\w* \w from His burning anger|strong="H2740"\w*. \w Therefore|strong="H5921"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w is called|strong="H7121"\w* \w the Valley|strong="H6010"\w* \w of Achor|strong="H5911"\w*\f + \fr 7:26 \fqa Achor \ft means \fqa trouble\ft .\f* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.
\c 8
\s1 The Conquest of Ai
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*, “\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w be afraid|strong="H3372"\w* \w or discouraged|strong="H2865"\w*. \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H4421"\w* \w with you|strong="H5973"\w*, \w and go up|strong="H6965"\w* \w and attack|strong="H5927"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \w See|strong="H7200"\w*, \w I have delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into your hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w his people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w his city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w his land|strong="H776"\w*. \v 2 \w And you shall do|strong="H6213"\w* \w to Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w and its king|strong="H4428"\w* \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w you did|strong="H6213"\w* \w to Jericho|strong="H3405"\w* \w and its king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w except that|strong="H7535"\w* \w you may carry off|strong="H962"\w* \w their plunder|strong="H7998"\w* \w and livestock|strong="H929"\w* for yourselves. \w Set up|strong="H7760"\w* \w an ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w behind|strong="H310"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H4421"\w* \w set out|strong="H6965"\w* \w to attack|strong="H5927"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w chose|strong="H977"\w* \w 30,000|strong="H7970"\w* \w mighty men|strong="H1368"\w* \w of valor|strong="H2428"\w* \w and sent them out|strong="H7971"\w* \w at night|strong="H3915"\w* \v 4 \w with these orders|strong="H6680"\w*: “\w Pay attention|strong="H7200"\w*. \w You|strong="H859"\w* \w are to lie in ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w behind|strong="H310"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w not|strong="H408"\w* \w too|strong="H3966"\w* \w far|strong="H7368"\w* \w from it|strong="H5892"\w*. \w All of you|strong="H3605"\w* \w must be|strong="H1961"\w* \w ready|strong="H3559"\w*. \v 5 \w Then I|strong="H589"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w with me|strong="H854"\w* \w will advance|strong="H7126"\w* \w on the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \w When|strong="H3588"\w* \w they come out|strong="H3318"\w* \w against us|strong="H7122"\w* \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w they did the first time|strong="H7223"\w*, \w we will flee|strong="H5127"\w* \w from them|strong="H6440"\w*. \v 6 \w They will pursue us|strong="H3318"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w we have drawn them away|strong="H5423"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w they will say|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w The Israelites are running away|strong="H5127"\w* \w from us|strong="H6440"\w* \w as they did before|strong="H834"\w*.’ \w So as we flee|strong="H5127"\w* \w from them|strong="H6440"\w*, \v 7 \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w are to rise|strong="H6965"\w* \w from the ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w and seize|strong="H3423"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w for the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w* \w will deliver it|strong="H5414"\w* \w into your hand|strong="H3027"\w*. \v 8 \w And|strong="H1961"\w* \w when you have taken|strong="H8610"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w set it|strong="H5892"\w* \w on fire|strong="H3341"\w*. \w Do|strong="H6213"\w* \w as the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has commanded|strong="H1697"\w*! \w See|strong="H7200"\w*, \w I have given you orders|strong="H6680"\w*.”
\p \v 9 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w sent them out|strong="H7971"\w*, \w and they went|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the place of ambush|strong="H3993"\w* \w and lay in wait|strong="H3427"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w Bethel|strong="H1008"\w* \w and|strong="H996"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w to the west|strong="H3220"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \w But Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w spent|strong="H3885"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w night|strong="H3915"\w* \w among|strong="H8432"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w got up early|strong="H7925"\w* \w the next morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w and mobilized|strong="H6485"\w* \w his men|strong="H5971"\w*, \w and he|strong="H1931"\w* \w and the elders|strong="H2205"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w marched|strong="H5927"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w them|strong="H5971"\w* \w up to Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \v 11 \w Then all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w who were|strong="H834"\w* \w with him|strong="H854"\w* \w marched up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and approached|strong="H5066"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \w They arrived|strong="H935"\w* \w in front of Ai|strong="H5048"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w to the north|strong="H6828"\w* \w of it|strong="H5857"\w*, \w with the valley|strong="H1516"\w* \w between them|strong="H996"\w* \w and the city|strong="H5857"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w Now Joshua had taken|strong="H3947"\w* \w about five|strong="H2568"\w* \w thousand|strong="H505"\w* \w men|strong="H376"\w* \w and set up|strong="H7760"\w* \w an ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w Bethel|strong="H1008"\w* \w and|strong="H996"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w to the west|strong="H3220"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \v 13 \w So the forces|strong="H5971"\w* \w were stationed|strong="H7760"\w* \w with the main|strong="H3605"\w* \w camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w to the north|strong="H6828"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w and the rear guard|strong="H6119"\w* \w to the west|strong="H3220"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \w And that|strong="H1931"\w* \w night|strong="H3915"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w went|strong="H1980"\w* \w into|strong="H8432"\w* \w the valley|strong="H6010"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w When the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w saw the Israelites|strong="H7200"\w*, \w he hurried|strong="H4116"\w* \w out|strong="H3318"\w* \w early in the morning|strong="H7925"\w* \w with the men|strong="H582"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w to engage|strong="H7122"\w* \w them|strong="H3478"\w* \w in battle|strong="H4421"\w* \w at an appointed place|strong="H4150"\w* \w overlooking|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Arabah|strong="H6160"\w*. \w But he|strong="H1931"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w know|strong="H3045"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w an ambush|strong="H693"\w* had been set up against him \w behind|strong="H310"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \v 15 \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w let themselves be beaten back|strong="H5060"\w* \w before them|strong="H6440"\w*, \w and they fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w toward|strong="H1870"\w* \w the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*. \v 16 \w Then all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H5971"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5892"\w* \w were summoned|strong="H2199"\w* \w to pursue them|strong="H7291"\w*, \w and they followed|strong="H7291"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and were drawn away|strong="H5423"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*. \v 17 \w Not|strong="H3808"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w was left|strong="H7604"\w* \w in Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w or Bethel|strong="H1008"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w go out|strong="H3318"\w* \w after|strong="H310"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w leaving|strong="H5800"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w wide open|strong="H6605"\w* \w while they pursued|strong="H7291"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*, “\w Hold out|strong="H5186"\w* \w your battle lance|strong="H3591"\w*\f + \fr 8:18 \ft Or \fqa javelin\ft ; twice in this verse, and also in verse 26\f* \w toward|strong="H413"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w into your hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w I will deliver the city|strong="H5414"\w*.” \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w held out|strong="H5186"\w* \w his battle lance|strong="H3591"\w* \w toward|strong="H413"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5892"\w*, \v 19 \w and as soon as he did so|strong="H5186"\w*, \w the men in ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w rose|strong="H6965"\w* \w quickly|strong="H4120"\w* \w from their position|strong="H4725"\w*. \w They rushed forward|strong="H7323"\w*, \w entered|strong="H935"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w captured it|strong="H3920"\w*, \w and immediately|strong="H4116"\w* \w set it|strong="H5892"\w* \w on fire|strong="H3341"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w When the men|strong="H582"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w turned|strong="H6437"\w* \w and looked|strong="H7200"\w* \w back|strong="H310"\w*, \w the smoke|strong="H6227"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was rising|strong="H5927"\w* \w into the sky|strong="H8064"\w*. \w They could not|strong="H3808"\w* \w escape|strong="H5127"\w* \w in any direction|strong="H2008"\w*, \w and the troops|strong="H5971"\w* \w who had fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w to the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w now turned|strong="H2015"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w their pursuers|strong="H7291"\w*. \v 21 \w When Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w the men in ambush|strong="H693"\w* \w had captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w and that|strong="H3588"\w* \w smoke|strong="H6227"\w* \w was rising from|strong="H5927"\w* \w it|strong="H5892"\w*, \w they turned around|strong="H7725"\w* \w and struck down|strong="H5221"\w* \w the men|strong="H582"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \v 22 \w Meanwhile, those in the ambush|strong="H428"\w* \w came out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w against them|strong="H7122"\w*, \w and the men of Ai were|strong="H1961"\w* \w trapped between|strong="H8432"\w* \w the Israelite|strong="H3478"\w* \w forces|strong="H428"\w* \w on|strong="H2088"\w* \w both sides|strong="H428"\w*. \w So Israel struck them down|strong="H5221"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w no|strong="H1115"\w* \w survivor|strong="H8300"\w* \w or fugitive|strong="H6412"\w* \w remained|strong="H7604"\w*. \v 23 \w But|strong="H853"\w* \w they took|strong="H8610"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w alive|strong="H2416"\w* \w and brought|strong="H7126"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*.
\p \v 24 \w When Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w had finished|strong="H3615"\w* \w killing|strong="H2026"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w who had pursued|strong="H7291"\w* them \w into the field|strong="H7704"\w* \w and wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*, \w and when every|strong="H3605"\w* \w last one of them had fallen|strong="H5307"\w* \w by the sword|strong="H2719"\w*, \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w* \w returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w to Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w and put|strong="H5221"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w to the sword as well|strong="H2719"\w*. \v 25 \w A total|strong="H3605"\w* \w of twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w thousand|strong="H505"\w* \w men|strong="H376"\w* \w and|strong="H5704"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w* \w fell|strong="H5307"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*— \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H582"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \v 26 \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w draw back|strong="H7725"\w* \w the hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w held|strong="H5186"\w* \w his battle lance|strong="H3591"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w he had devoted to destruction|strong="H2763"\w*\f + \fr 8:26 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w who lived|strong="H3427"\w* \w in Ai|strong="H5857"\w*. \v 27 \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w took|strong="H962"\w* for themselves \w only|strong="H7535"\w* \w the cattle|strong="H929"\w* \w and plunder|strong="H7998"\w* \w of that|strong="H1931"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w as the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*.
\p \v 28 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w burned|strong="H8313"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*\f + \fr 8:28 \fqa Ai \ft means \fqa ruin\ft .\f* \w and made it|strong="H7760"\w* \w a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w heap of ruins|strong="H8510"\w*, \w a desolation|strong="H8077"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*. \v 29 \w He hung|strong="H8518"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w a tree|strong="H6086"\w*\f + \fr 8:29 \ft Or \fqa He impaled the king of Ai on a pole\f* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w evening|strong="H6153"\w*, \w and at sunset|strong="H935"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w that they take down the body|strong="H5038"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the tree|strong="H6086"\w* \w and throw it down|strong="H7993"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w of the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w gate|strong="H8179"\w*. \w And over it|strong="H5921"\w* \w they raised|strong="H6965"\w* \w a large|strong="H1419"\w* \w pile|strong="H1530"\w* \w of rocks|strong="H68"\w*, \w which remains to|strong="H5704"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.
\s1 Joshua Renews the Covenant
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 27:1–10|DEU 27:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 30 \w At that time|strong="H227"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w built|strong="H1129"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w on Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Ebal|strong="H5858"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \v 31 \w just as|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w the servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*. \w He built it according to what is written|strong="H3789"\w* \w in the Book|strong="H5612"\w* \w of the Law|strong="H8451"\w* \w of Moses|strong="H4872"\w*: “\w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of uncut|strong="H8003"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w no|strong="H3808"\w* \w iron tool|strong="H1270"\w* \w has been used|strong="H5130"\w*.”\f + \fr 8:31 \ft \ref Exodus 20:25|EXO 20:25\ref*; Deuteronomy 27:5\f* \w And on it|strong="H5921"\w* \w they offered|strong="H5927"\w* \w burnt offerings|strong="H5930"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and they sacrificed|strong="H2076"\w* \w peace offerings|strong="H8002"\w*.
\p \v 32 \w And there|strong="H8033"\w* \w in the presence|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w*, \w Joshua inscribed|strong="H3789"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the stones|strong="H68"\w* \w a copy|strong="H4932"\w* \w of the law|strong="H8451"\w* \w of Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w he had written|strong="H3789"\w*. \v 33 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w foreigners|strong="H1616"\w* \w and citizens alike|strong="H249"\w*, \w with their elders|strong="H2205"\w*, \w officers|strong="H7860"\w*, \w and judges|strong="H8199"\w*, \w stood|strong="H5975"\w* \w on both sides|strong="H2088"\w* \w of the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w facing|strong="H5048"\w* \w the Levitical|strong="H3881"\w* \w priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w who carried|strong="H5375"\w* \w it|strong="H727"\w*. \w Half of the people stood|strong="H2677"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w front|strong="H4136"\w* \w of Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Gerizim|strong="H1630"\w* \w and half of them|strong="H2677"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w front|strong="H4136"\w* \w of Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Ebal|strong="H5858"\w*, \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w the servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w earlier|strong="H7223"\w*, \w to bless|strong="H1288"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
\p \v 34 \w Afterward|strong="H310"\w*, \w Joshua read aloud|strong="H7121"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the law|strong="H8451"\w*— \w the blessings|strong="H1293"\w* \w and the curses|strong="H7045"\w*— \w according to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that is written|strong="H3789"\w* \w in the Book|strong="H5612"\w* \w of the Law|strong="H8451"\w*. \v 35 \w There was|strong="H1961"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w a word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w failed|strong="H3808"\w* \w to read|strong="H7121"\w* \w before|strong="H5048"\w* \w the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w assembly|strong="H6951"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w including the women|strong="H802"\w*, \w the little ones|strong="H2945"\w*, \w and the foreigners|strong="H1616"\w* \w who lived|strong="H1980"\w* \w among them|strong="H7130"\w*.
\c 9
\s1 The Deceit of the Gibeonites
\p \v 1 \w Now when|strong="H1961"\w* \w news of this reached|strong="H8085"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w west|strong="H5676"\w* \w of the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* — \w those|strong="H834"\w* \w in the hill country|strong="H2022"\w*, \w the foothills|strong="H8219"\w*,\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w along the coast|strong="H2348"\w* \w of the Great|strong="H1419"\w* \w Sea|strong="H3220"\w*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea\f* \w toward|strong="H413"\w* \w Lebanon|strong="H3844"\w* (\w the Hittites|strong="H2850"\w*, \w Amorites|strong="H567"\w*, \w Canaanites|strong="H3669"\w*, \w Perizzites|strong="H6522"\w*, \w Hivites|strong="H2340"\w*, \w and Jebusites|strong="H2983"\w*)— \v 2 \w they came|strong="H6908"\w* \w together|strong="H3162"\w* \w to wage war|strong="H3898"\w* \w against|strong="H5973"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w But the people|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*, \w having heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w had done|strong="H6213"\w* \w to Jericho|strong="H3405"\w* \w and Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \v 4 \w acted deceptively|strong="H6213"\w* \w and set out|strong="H1980"\w* \w as envoys|strong="H6737"\w*,\f + \fr 9:4 \ft Or \fqa set out with provisions\f* \w carrying|strong="H3947"\w* \w on their donkeys|strong="H2543"\w* \w worn-out|strong="H1087"\w* \w sacks|strong="H8242"\w* \w and old|strong="H1087"\w* \w wineskins|strong="H4997"\w*, \w cracked|strong="H1234"\w* \w and mended|strong="H6887"\w*. \v 5 \w They put worn|strong="H1087"\w*, \w patched|strong="H2921"\w* \w sandals|strong="H5275"\w* \w on their feet|strong="H7272"\w* \w and threadbare|strong="H1087"\w* \w clothing|strong="H8008"\w* \w on their bodies|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and their whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w supply|strong="H6718"\w* \w of bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w was dry|strong="H3001"\w* \w and moldy|strong="H5350"\w*. \v 6 \w They went|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w at Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w* \w and|strong="H413"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, “\w We have come|strong="H935"\w* \w from a distant|strong="H7350"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w*; \w please make|strong="H3772"\w* \w a treaty|strong="H1285"\w*\f + \fr 9:6 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft ; also in verses 7, 11, 15, and 16.\f* with us.”
\p \v 7 \w But the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Hivites|strong="H2340"\w*, “\w Perhaps|strong="H194"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w dwell|strong="H3427"\w* \w near us|strong="H7130"\w*. \w How|strong="H349"\w* \w can we make|strong="H3772"\w* \w a treaty with you|strong="H1285"\w*?”
\p \v 8 “\w We|strong="H587"\w* \w are your servants|strong="H5650"\w*,” \w they said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*.
\p \w Then Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w asked them|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Who|strong="H4310"\w* \w are you|strong="H859"\w* \w and where|strong="H370"\w* \w have you come from|strong="H935"\w*?”
\p \v 9 “\w Your servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w have come|strong="H935"\w* \w from a very|strong="H3966"\w* \w distant|strong="H7350"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w*,” \w they replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w because of the fame|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w*. \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w we have heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w the reports about Him|strong="H8089"\w*: \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w He did|strong="H6213"\w* \w in Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \v 10 \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w He did|strong="H6213"\w* \w to the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of the Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w beyond|strong="H5676"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*— \w Sihon|strong="H5511"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Heshbon|strong="H2809"\w* \w and Og|strong="H5747"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Bashan|strong="H1316"\w*, \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w reigned in Ashtaroth|strong="H6252"\w*. \v 11 \w So the elders|strong="H2205"\w* \w and|strong="H3605"\w* \w inhabitants|strong="H3427"\w* \w of our land|strong="H776"\w* \w told|strong="H559"\w* \w us|strong="H413"\w*, ‘\w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w provisions|strong="H6720"\w* \w for your journey|strong="H1870"\w*; \w go|strong="H1980"\w* \w to meet them|strong="H7122"\w* \w and say|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*: \w We|strong="H587"\w* \w are your servants|strong="H5650"\w*. \w Please make|strong="H3772"\w* \w a treaty|strong="H1285"\w* with us.’
\p \v 12 \w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w of ours was warm|strong="H2525"\w* \w when we packed|strong="H6679"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w at home|strong="H1004"\w* \w on the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w we left|strong="H3318"\w* \w to come|strong="H1980"\w* \w to you|strong="H413"\w*. \w But look|strong="H2009"\w*, \w it is now|strong="H6258"\w* \w dry|strong="H3001"\w* \w and|strong="H1961"\w* \w moldy|strong="H5350"\w*. \v 13 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w wineskins|strong="H4997"\w* \w were new|strong="H2319"\w* \w when we filled|strong="H4390"\w* \w them|strong="H834"\w*, \w but look|strong="H2009"\w*, \w they are cracked|strong="H1234"\w*. \w And these|strong="H428"\w* \w clothes|strong="H8008"\w* \w and sandals|strong="H5275"\w* \w are worn out|strong="H1086"\w* \w from our very|strong="H3966"\w* \w long|strong="H7230"\w* \w journey|strong="H1870"\w*.”
\p \v 14 \w Then the men of Israel|strong="H582"\w* \w sampled|strong="H3947"\w* \w their provisions|strong="H6718"\w* \w but did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w seek|strong="H7592"\w* \w the counsel|strong="H6310"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 15 \w And Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* \w a treaty|strong="H1285"\w* \w of peace|strong="H7965"\w* with them \w to let them live|strong="H2421"\w*, \w and the leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w of the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w swore an oath|strong="H7650"\w* to them.
\p \v 16 \w Three|strong="H7969"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w after|strong="H310"\w* \w they had made|strong="H3772"\w* \w the treaty|strong="H1285"\w* with the Gibeonites, \w the Israelites learned|strong="H8085"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w they were|strong="H1992"\w* \w neighbors|strong="H7138"\w*, \w living|strong="H3427"\w* \w among them|strong="H7130"\w*. \v 17 \w So the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w and on the third|strong="H7992"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w arrived|strong="H935"\w* \w at their cities|strong="H5892"\w* — \w Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*, \w Chephirah|strong="H3716"\w*, \w Beeroth|strong="H881"\w*, \w and Kiriath-jearim|strong="H7157"\w*. \v 18 \w But the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w attack them|strong="H5221"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w of the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w had sworn an oath|strong="H7650"\w* to them \w by the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w And the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w grumbled|strong="H3885"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H5387"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w answered|strong="H559"\w*, “\w We|strong="H587"\w* \w have sworn an oath|strong="H7650"\w* to them \w by the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and now|strong="H6258"\w* \w we cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w touch|strong="H5060"\w* them. \v 20 \w This|strong="H2063"\w* \w is how we will treat|strong="H6213"\w* them: \w We will let them live|strong="H2421"\w*, \w so that no|strong="H3808"\w* \w wrath|strong="H7110"\w* \w will fall|strong="H1961"\w* \w on us|strong="H5921"\w* \w because of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the oath|strong="H7621"\w* \w we swore|strong="H7650"\w* to them.” \v 21 \w They|strong="H5387"\w* \w continued|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Let them live|strong="H2421"\w*, \w but let them be|strong="H1961"\w* \w woodcutters|strong="H2404"\w* \w and water|strong="H4325"\w* \w carriers|strong="H7579"\w* \w for the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w*.” \w So|strong="H834"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w kept their promise|strong="H1696"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w Then Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w summoned|strong="H7121"\w* the Gibeonites \w and said|strong="H1696"\w*, “\w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w did you deceive|strong="H7411"\w* \w us|strong="H853"\w* \w by telling us|strong="H559"\w* \w you live far away|strong="H7350"\w* from \w us|strong="H587"\w*, \w when in fact you|strong="H859"\w* \w live|strong="H3427"\w* \w among us|strong="H7130"\w*? \v 23 \w Now therefore|strong="H6258"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w are under a curse|strong="H779"\w* \w and will perpetually|strong="H3808"\w* \w serve|strong="H5650"\w* \w as woodcutters|strong="H2404"\w* \w and water|strong="H4325"\w* \w carriers|strong="H7579"\w* \w for the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of my God|strong="H430"\w*.”
\p \v 24 \w The Gibeonites answered|strong="H6030"\w*, “\w Your servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w were told clearly|strong="H5046"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w* \w had commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w His servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w to give|strong="H5414"\w* you \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w and wipe out|strong="H8045"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its inhabitants|strong="H3427"\w* \w before you|strong="H6440"\w*. \w So we greatly|strong="H3966"\w* \w feared|strong="H3372"\w* \w for our lives|strong="H5315"\w* \w because of you|strong="H6440"\w*, \w and that is why we have done|strong="H6213"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w*. \v 25 \w Now|strong="H6258"\w* \w we are in your hands|strong="H3027"\w*. \w Do|strong="H6213"\w* to us \w whatever seems|strong="H5869"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* \w and right|strong="H3477"\w* \w to you|strong="H6213"\w*.”
\p \v 26 \w So|strong="H3651"\w* \w Joshua did this|strong="H6213"\w* \w and delivered|strong="H5337"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w from the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w*, \w and they did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w kill the Gibeonites|strong="H2026"\w*. \v 27 \w On that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w he|strong="H3091"\w* \w made them|strong="H5414"\w* \w woodcutters|strong="H2404"\w* \w and water|strong="H4325"\w* \w carriers|strong="H7579"\w*, \w as they are to this day|strong="H5704"\w* \w for the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w and for the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the place|strong="H4725"\w* \w He would choose|strong="H977"\w*.
\c 10
\s1 The Day the Sun Stood Still
\p \v 1 \w Now|strong="H1961"\w* \w Adoni-zedek|strong="H139"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w had captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w and devoted it to destruction|strong="H2763"\w*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 28, 35, 37, 39, and 40.\f* — \w doing to|strong="H6213"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w* \w and its king|strong="H4428"\w* \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w he had done to|strong="H6213"\w* \w Jericho|strong="H3405"\w* \w and its king|strong="H4428"\w* — \w and that|strong="H3588"\w* \w the people|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w* \w had made peace|strong="H7999"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w and were living|strong="H1961"\w* \w near them|strong="H7130"\w*. \v 2 \w So Adoni-zedek and his people were greatly|strong="H3966"\w* \w alarmed|strong="H3372"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w* \w was a great|strong="H1419"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w like one|strong="H259"\w* \w of the royal|strong="H4467"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w*; \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w was larger|strong="H1419"\w* \w than|strong="H4480"\w* \w Ai|strong="H5857"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its men|strong="H582"\w* \w were mighty|strong="H1368"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w Therefore Adoni-zedek|strong="H139"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w word to|strong="H413"\w* \w Hoham|strong="H1944"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Hebron|strong="H2275"\w*, \w Piram|strong="H6502"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Jarmuth|strong="H3412"\w*, \w Japhia|strong="H3309"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Lachish|strong="H3923"\w*, \w and Debir|strong="H1688"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Eglon|strong="H5700"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, \v 4 “\w Come up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and help me|strong="H5826"\w*. \w We will attack|strong="H5221"\w* \w Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w they have made peace|strong="H7999"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*.”
\p \v 5 \w So the five|strong="H2568"\w* \w kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of the Amorites|strong="H567"\w*— \w the kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w Hebron|strong="H2275"\w*, \w Jarmuth|strong="H3412"\w*, \w Lachish|strong="H3923"\w*, \w and Eglon|strong="H5700"\w*— \w joined forces|strong="H622"\w* \w and advanced|strong="H5927"\w* \w with all|strong="H3605"\w* \w their armies|strong="H4264"\w*. \w They camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w before|strong="H5921"\w* \w Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w* \w and made war|strong="H3898"\w* \w against it|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w Then the men|strong="H582"\w* \w of Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w word to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w at Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w*: “\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w abandon|strong="H7503"\w* \w your servants|strong="H5650"\w*. \w Come|strong="H5927"\w* \w quickly|strong="H4120"\w* \w and save|strong="H3467"\w* us! \w Help us|strong="H5826"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of the Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w from|strong="H3427"\w* \w the hill country|strong="H2022"\w* \w have joined forces|strong="H6908"\w* \w against us|strong="H413"\w*.”
\p \v 7 \w So Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w and his whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H4421"\w*, \w including all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the mighty men|strong="H1368"\w* \w of valor|strong="H2428"\w*, \w came|strong="H5927"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*, “\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w be afraid|strong="H3372"\w* of them, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w I have delivered them|strong="H5414"\w* \w into your hand|strong="H3027"\w*. \w Not|strong="H3808"\w* \w one|strong="H376"\w* of them \w shall stand|strong="H5975"\w* \w against you|strong="H6440"\w*.”
\p \v 9 \w After marching|strong="H5927"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w night|strong="H3915"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w*, \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w caught|strong="H935"\w* \w them|strong="H413"\w* \w by surprise|strong="H6597"\w*. \v 10 \w And the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w threw them into confusion|strong="H2000"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w who defeated them|strong="H5221"\w* \w in a great|strong="H1419"\w* \w slaughter|strong="H4347"\w* \w at Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*, \w pursued them|strong="H7291"\w* \w along|strong="H1870"\w* \w the ascent|strong="H4608"\w* \w to Beth-horon|strong="H1032"\w*, \w and struck them down|strong="H5221"\w* \w as|strong="H5704"\w* \w far as Azekah|strong="H5825"\w* \w and Makkedah|strong="H4719"\w*. \v 11 \w As they fled|strong="H5127"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w along the descent|strong="H4174"\w* \w from Beth-horon|strong="H1032"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w Azekah|strong="H5825"\w*, \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w cast down|strong="H7993"\w* \w on them|strong="H5921"\w* \w large|strong="H1419"\w* \w hailstones|strong="H68"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the sky|strong="H8064"\w*, \w and more|strong="H7227"\w* \w of them|strong="H834"\w* \w were killed|strong="H4191"\w* \w by|strong="H68"\w* \w the hailstones|strong="H1259"\w* \w than|strong="H834"\w* \w by the swords|strong="H2719"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w On the day that|strong="H3117"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w gave the Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w over|strong="H5414"\w* \w to|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w spoke|strong="H1696"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w in the presence|strong="H5869"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*:
\b 
\q1 “\w O sun|strong="H8121"\w*, \w stand still|strong="H1826"\w* \w over Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*,
\q2 \w O moon|strong="H3394"\w*, \w over the Valley|strong="H6010"\w* \w of Aijalon|strong="H357"\w*.”\f + \fr 10:12 \ft See \ref Jasher 88:63|88:63\ref*.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \w So the sun|strong="H8121"\w* \w stood still|strong="H1826"\w*
\q2 \w and the moon|strong="H3394"\w* \w stopped|strong="H5975"\w*
\q1 \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the nation|strong="H1471"\w* \w took vengeance|strong="H5358"\w*
\q2 \w upon its enemies|strong="H341"\w*.\f + \fr 10:13 \ft Or \fqa triumphed over its enemies\f*
\p \w Is this|strong="H1931"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w written|strong="H3789"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Book|strong="H5612"\w* \w of Jashar|strong="H3477"\w*?\f + \fr 10:13 \ft Or \fqa the Book of the Upright One\ft , commonly cited as \fqa Jasher\f*
\b 
\q1 “\w So the sun|strong="H8121"\w* \w stopped|strong="H5975"\w*
\q2 \w in the middle|strong="H2677"\w* \w of the sky|strong="H8064"\w*
\q1 \w and delayed|strong="H3808"\w* \w going down|strong="H935"\w*
\q2 \w about a full|strong="H8549"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.”\f + \fr 10:13 \ft See \ref Jasher 88:64|88:64\ref*.\f*
\p \v 14 \w There has been|strong="H1961"\w* \w no|strong="H3808"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w like it before|strong="H6440"\w* \w or since|strong="H310"\w*, \w when the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w listened|strong="H8085"\w* \w to the voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w of a man|strong="H376"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w fought|strong="H3898"\w* \w for Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
