\p \v 10 \w At that|strong="H1931"\w* \w time|strong="H6256"\w* \w Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w turned back|strong="H7725"\w* \w and captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w Hazor|strong="H2674"\w* \w and put|strong="H5221"\w* \w its king|strong="H4428"\w* \w to the sword|strong="H2719"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w Hazor|strong="H2674"\w* \w was|strong="H1931"\w* \w formerly|strong="H6440"\w* \w the head|strong="H7218"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w kingdoms|strong="H4467"\w*. \v 11 \w The Israelites put|strong="H5221"\w* \w everyone|strong="H3605"\w* in Hazor \w to the sword|strong="H2719"\w*, \w devoting them to destruction|strong="H2763"\w*.\f + \fr 11:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 12, 20, and 21.\f* \w Nothing|strong="H3808"\w* \w that breathed|strong="H5397"\w* \w remained|strong="H3498"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w Joshua burned down|strong="H8313"\w* \w Hazor itself|strong="H2674"\w*.
