\p \v 20 \w Was not|strong="H3808"\w* \w Achan|strong="H5912"\w*\f + \fr 22:20 \fqa Achan \ft means \fqa troubler\ft ; also called \fqa Achar\ft in \ref 1 Chronicles 2:7|1CH 2:7\ref*.\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zerah|strong="H2226"\w* \w unfaithful|strong="H4603"\w* \w regarding|strong="H4604"\w* \w what was set apart for destruction|strong="H2764"\w*,\f + \fr 22:20 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \w bringing wrath|strong="H7110"\w* \w upon|strong="H5921"\w* \w the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*? \w Yet it was not|strong="H3808"\w* \w only|strong="H259"\w* \w Achan|strong="H1931"\w* \w who perished|strong="H1478"\w* \w because of his sin|strong="H5771"\w*!’”
